    "created_at": "2022-07-18T17:11:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-07-18T17:11:41Z",
    "body": "I'm pretty sure this is not specific to Web Serial.\r\n\r\nIIRC, for USB CDC-ACM interfaces, zero-length packets are normal signaling mechanism and your application should be able to tolerate receiving them. And if your device is sending data, you may need to make sure that you send ZLPs as needed to avoid the case where it gets \"stuck\" when sending a multiple of the endpoint packet size.\r\n\r\nIt's been a while since I've reread the USB spec, so I'll leave it to other [StackOverflow answers](https://electronics.stackexchange.com/questions/253669/usb-cdc-help-with-zero-packets) and [online resources](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/rtos/usbx/usbx-device-stack-5#general-considerations-for-bulk-transfer) to go over the details.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
